            <ArticleTitle>Technique of coronary angiography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>781-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new manufacturing process and new shapes of the left and right catheters for coronary angiography by the transfemoral route increase the safety of the examination by reducing the time and avoiding the risks involved in catheter occlusion of the arteries. The simultaneous filling of the sinus and the whole coronary artery from its origin increases the anatomic information. Pressure-monitoring is unnecessary.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
